This product includes or uses the following third-party material.

1. OCR models (embedded in the default CLI build)
   PaddleOCR PP-OCRv5 mobile det and cyrillic PP-OCRv5 mobile rec, with its
   character dictionary. Copyright (c) PaddlePaddle Authors. Apache License 2.0.
   Unmodified ONNX files; sources and sha256 in crates/ocr/model-manifest.txt.
   ONNX Runtime (Microsoft, MIT) and its bundled components, and Rust crates
   whose licenses require a notice in binary form: see crates/ocr/NOTICE and
   crates/ocr/licenses/.

2. Need-OCR letter-bigram table (crates/formats/data/need_ocr/bigrams.json)
   Counted from public-domain Russian texts of ru.wikisource.org and from the
   ground-truth Markdown of opendataloader-bench (Apache License 2.0), which is
   based on the DP-Bench dataset (Upstage, MIT). The table holds only letter-pair
   frequencies, no document text. Details: crates/formats/data/need_ocr/NOTICE.

3. Docling (https://github.com/docling-project/docling, MIT)
   Some heading heuristics (heading levels from numbering and style, titles
   from the PDF outline) follow the logic of Docling 2.148, and Docling output
   was used as a reference when evaluating headings and tables. No Docling code
   was copied; it is credited here as a source of ideas.

4. pdf_oxide (https://github.com/fixcik/pdf_oxide, a fork of
   https://github.com/yfedoseev/pdf_oxide)
   Used as a git dependency pinned to a commit of the fork.
   Copyright (c) 2025-present Yury Fedoseev and the PDFOxide project
   contributors. Dual-licensed under MIT OR Apache License 2.0.

5. Test fixtures
   - crates/formats/tests/fixtures/office/poi: files from Apache POI test-data
     (https://github.com/apache/poi/tree/trunk/test-data), Apache License 2.0.
     See the NOTICE file in that directory. crates/formats/tests/fixtures/office/
     expected holds plaindoc output for these files and the generated ones.
   - All other fixtures are synthetic: generated by scripts in scripts/
     (forms, resumes, tables) and crates/formats/tests/fixtures/pdf/gen.sh, by
